{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1447981-difficulty-at-using-gifts","id":1447981,"title":"Difficulty at using Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-08T13:48:01-07:00","id":1447981,"title":"Difficulty at using Gifts","content":"So, some Gifts are almost impossible to use due to their difficulty on the activation roll. Some examples are Stench and the City from the Book of the City is diff Stamina + 5 and Fenris' Bite from W20 is Stamina + 3. A Garou in Crinos with a total Stamina rating of 8 is immune? Are there some other rules besides houserules to make the difficulty more balanced and rewarding to the user of the Gift as providing a good chance of defense for the receiving end?<br /> <br /> Thank you all, stay safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","user":"Fenixpp","date":". 05-08-2021, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T15:21:34-07:00","id":1447990,"title":"","content":"WtA Gift difficulties are frequently strangely high for the math of the system... not just the ones that do these sorts of calculations. After W20, it's just sort been accepted as the way things are until we get an edition that's focused on a more significant overhaul of the mechanics.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm having trouble finding a specific official source for this, but my brain keeps insisting there is one, so hopefully someone else can remember why I think that. But, IIRC, you use your base Homid stats for things like this, not your form modified ones. So at least against other werewolves and humans, Fenris' Bite never goes above 8 (maybe 9 with a specific Totem). Of course once you start getting into WtA baddies that are stated with 6+ Attributes, or other WoD critters, you still get back to the same issue.<br /> <br /> Also, you can still roll at difficulty 10, it just is a very bad idea because the math gets very harsh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T15:33:46-07:00","id":1447992,"title":"","content":"Wow... now that you said this I'm very curious to this reference of using Attributes without the form bonuses. I only have books from WTA and I can search on the ST guides, but I'm afraid that this reference isn't in there. If I find it I'll post here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T15:54:42-07:00","id":1447995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1447981-difficulty-at-using-gifts?p=1447990#post1447990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Of course once you start getting into WtA baddies that are stated with 6+ Attributes, or other WoD critters, you still get back to the same issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also imagine approaching this through the drama of the scene, enemies with such high Stamina cannot be attacked with Fenris' Bite straight ahead, they must be put in a position in a fight (subdued on the floor, held up to target the limb better and so on) to reduce the difficulty at using the Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-08T16:41:49-07:00","id":1447998,"title":"","content":"I'm worried it's something that one of the devs said on the forums or something like that rather than something in the books, which is why I can't remember a book to look at.<br /> <br /> While you could claim it falls under general rules (it would be a huge stretch and I'd consider it a house rule) to reduce the difficulty of Gifts in a situational fashion like that, it would be a functional (and something you could do more comprehensively) way to make some of these Gifts more useful; esp. something like Fenris Bite given the fact that it's a Rank 5 Gift and you still need to bite the target.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T01:22:51-07:00","id":1448029,"title":"","content":"MtA revised had, iirc, rules to turn difficulties above 9 into an successes threshold. It would make WtA work better, too.<br /> Still, the whole adjustment of difficulties works only good between 5 and 8, imo. And I guess that is why the systems of newer games (CoD) have been turned into a solid target number and dice pool adjustments, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T02:07:16-07:00","id":1448034,"title":"","content":"The Threshold rules are in M20 as well.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how much they would do for Gifts though. Threshold generally works for Mage because it's meant for a magic system that requires very few successes relative to the results, and you can perform difficult effects as rituals to make them extended casting to help make up for the increased success requirements Thresholds apply, and generally mage can spend WP on every casting roll to help offset things further. For Gifts where it's roll once to activate the power, you're not necessarily making things better than rolling at diff 10 (and spending a WP if the Gift doesn't require one to activate it too).<br /> <br /> While the CofD focuses on modifying dice-pools with a static TN, it's not the only approach (Exalted 3e, Storypath and V5 do it differently to the CofD and each other). The big lesson that goes back to the late 90s and the first edition of the Aeon/Trinity games is that the WoD has too many dials to modify how hard a task is: the TN can change, the dice-pool can change, and the number of successes achieved/needed can change. It's very hard to justify all three as representing different forms of changes in how hard something is to do. The reason to drop TN manipulation is that it's the variable that causes the most difficult to intuit results on the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T02:32:04-07:00","id":1448038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1447981-difficulty-at-using-gifts?p=1448034#post1448034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason to drop TN manipulation is that it's the variable that causes the most difficult to intuit results on the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-09T04:44:00-07:00","id":1448041,"title":"","content":"After searching a lot Heavy Arms, I couldn't find the official reference, but I thank you for your time.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the insight you all. I already use V5 combat rules in my WTA games to smooth things out and get use to it when W5 arrives. I decided to house rule/golden rule that this kind of Gifts will be a resisted roll, in the case of Fenris Bite it will be Strength + Primal-Urge vs Stamina +3 of the target. I believe this even things out. When W5 arrives at least I will have the base dice pools to house rule again in the case of Gifts that don't get reprinted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T08:58:26-07:00","id":1448227,"title":"","content":"I haven't been able to look, but I seem to remember this being explicit in W:tA first edition. I remember reading it and thinking &quot;well, I'll just ignore that&quot; since I was so focused on getting the best play experience FOR werewolves, not necessarily AGAINST werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}